  "answer": "Project Zenith is a major initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000 for phase one, led by Sarah Tan. The project has seen significant team expansion, including the addition of five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, as well as specific hires like Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with user interface enhancements planned for October. The project focuses on leveraging AI to enhance data visualization tools and predictive analytics, with initial findings suggesting a potential 20% increase in efficiency. A call for ideas from R&D was issued with a July 20th deadline. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective from January next year. Progress updates and detailed reports are scheduled for staff meetings in August, September, and November."
